ud services.\\n- Apply least‑privilege principles for file and folder permissions.\\n\\n## Email & Phishing\\n- Verify sender addresses and hover over links before clicking.\\n- Do not open attachments from unknown sources.\\n- Report suspicious emails to your IT/security team.\\n\\n## Software & Application Security\\n- Install software only from trusted sources or official app stores.\\n- Review application permissions and revoke unnecessary access.\\n- Use sandboxing or containerization for high‑risk applications when possible.\\n\\n## Incident Response\\n- Keep a list of critical accounts and recovery options (recovery email, phone).\\n- If a breach is suspected, change passwords immediately and enable MFA.\\n- Document the incident, steps taken, and lessons learned for future improvement.\\n\\n## Continuous Improvement\\n- Conduct periodic security reviews (quarterly for personal, monthly for organizations

